      <div type="clause" n="71.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 71.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>And cingces<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.6"/> þegnes heregeata inne mid Denu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>, þe his socne hæbbe: IIII pund.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>And kyncges ðegnes heregeata inne mid Denum, ðe his socne hæbbe: IIII pund.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="358" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ cyninges þegnes heregeata<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.3-2"/> inne mid Denum, þe his socne habbe: IIII pund.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.10"/> táini regis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.11"/> releuatio cum Dacis, qui sócnam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.12"/> habet: IIII<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.13"/> lib.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.3-3"/><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Liberalis hominis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.4"/> qui habet consuetudines suas<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.5"/>, quem Angli dicunt kinges þegen, debitum post mortem eius, quod supra nominauimus heregeat: IIII librę<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.6-2"/>;</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="71.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Et uirronis excercitualia apud Danos, qui suum priuilegium habeat: quatuor libre.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="71a.3" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="210" ed="#robertson"/>And kyncges ðegnes heregeata inne mid Denum ðe his socne hæbbe—IIII pund.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And cingces þegnes heregeata inne mid Denum, þe his socne hæbbe: IIII pund.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="359" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.de.1"/> im Lande bei den Dänen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.de.2"/> das Heergewæte eines Königsthegn, der seine Gerichtsimmunität<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_71-3.lnote.de.3"/> besitzt: 4 Pfund [Silber].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And in the land among the Danes, the heriot of a king's thegn who has his own jurisdiction: 4 pounds [of silver].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="211" ed="#robertson"/>And among the Danes the heriot of a king's thegn who possesses rights of jurisdiction shall be £4.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="472" ed="#whitelock"/>And the heriot of the king’s thegn among the Danes, who has right of jurisdiction; four pounds.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="291" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And the tribute paid in the Danelaw by a king’s thane who possesses jurisdictional rights over his property shall be four pounds.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 359, October 2026 (MS Cons); AU: corrected against Rabin p. 290 / 291, October 2026 (was “iiii”, now “IIII”)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">habeant <hi rend="italic">Hr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">habeant Hr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">71, 3 <hi rend="italic">fehlt Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">71, 3 lacking in Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sacham habeat <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> suam <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Hn</hi> 14, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sacham habeat K; suam added by Hn 14, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">IIII — regi <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">IIII — regi lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyninges <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyninges Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">358</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verbessert aus</hi> -gata</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corrected from -gata</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">71,1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt;</hi> 71,3 <hi rend="italic">ff. steht vor</hi> 71, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">71,1 lacking; 71,3 ff. stands before 71, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">homo, <hi rend="italic">am Rande</hi> hominis <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">homo, in the margin hominis Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb, wo</hi> quas</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb, where quas</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.oe.6-2" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">359</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">li' <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">li' Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">71, 3ff. benutzt durch Hn 14, 4, der zweimal dem Agsächs. näher als Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">71, 3ff. used by Hn 14, 4, who is twice closer to the Anglo-Saxon than Q</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diese partikulare Beschränkung fehlt Inst wohl nur zufällig, nicht etwa, weil (nach Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 114) das Heergewäte bei Dänen erst über England eindrang</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This regional restriction is probably missing from Inst merely by chance, not, say, because (according to Steenstrup <hi rend="italic">Danelag</hi> 114) the heriot reached the Danes only by way of England</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_71-3.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">212</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Justizertrag allein’ Adams (<hi rend="italic">Essays</hi> 43) zu eng; ‘baronial court’ Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 99) nur im Ausdruck zu modern für ‘private Gerichtsbarkeit’; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 24b. 27</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Profits of justice alone’ Adams (<hi rend="italic">Essays</hi> 43), too narrow; ‘baronial court’ Kemble (<hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 99), too modern only in expression, for ‘private jurisdiction’; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 24b. 27</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
